{"id": "EUVD-2026-59220", "enisaUuid": "9236c1f4-4cbe-3e29-82c8-a48093ac1982", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv4: igmp: Fix potential memory leaks in igmp_mod_timer() and igmp_stop_timer()\n\nWhen a timer is deleted and not re-armed in igmp_mod_timer(), or stopped\nin igmp_stop_timer(), the code currently decrements the reference counter\nof the multicast list entry @im using refcount_dec(&im->refcnt).\n\nHowever, both functions can be called from the RCU reader path:\n- igmp_mod_timer() via igmp_heard_query() -> for_each_pmc_rcu()\n- igmp_stop_timer() via igmp_rcv() -> igmp_heard_report()\n\nIf the group im was concurrently removed from the list by ip_mc_dec_group(),\nits reference count might have already been decremented to 1.\n\nIn this case, timer_delete() succeeds, and refcount_dec() decrements\nthe refcount from 1 to 0. Since refcount_dec() does not free the object\nwhen it hits 0 (unlike ip_ma_put()), the im structure is leaked.\n\nFix this by using ip_ma_put(im) instead of refcount_dec(&im->refcnt),\nand deferring the put until after the spinlock is released.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d0effadf8d2cc9d006e4c4ab0ab6737aed28d77", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40d6360ccf9bcbe17b5cb248a84e8e004aac2faa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f60ec3058a85447008b88b762c859d336163acb3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/95128dc74425ec19ed4f2077ccc651e791ff4b75", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3546deaa0c30a14c7cdb5dc8f2432cb428f0cd36"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72321", "GHSA-mrw5-54xq-r399"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3647aae2-7695-381e-9d87-440e6bd2efa6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "4b8f7b70-6ec4-31e0-9586-0eff6060490e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "532a4c1b-fb52-3e67-8cc2-9148b9148f36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "594bddc5-8183-347f-afe6-05b35605bf34", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <40d6360ccf9bcbe17b5cb248a84e8e004aac2faa"}, {"id": "70d8f8f8-66cc-3fbf-bf3e-43ac821cfdde", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "792e0355-eb5b-3fab-8588-3920d4d30f51", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "a1d44a51-8a3a-307d-b4d5-dac7a83b1876", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <2d0effadf8d2cc9d006e4c4ab0ab6737aed28d77"}, {"id": "c3d9c361-94b8-3a03-b9c4-17b83e8dda12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <95128dc74425ec19ed4f2077ccc651e791ff4b75"}, {"id": "c91c6bc1-3ac3-313a-9740-0bb98cf4c6cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "cfbf62a0-03ed-39a5-8908-31b82928e99e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <3546deaa0c30a14c7cdb5dc8f2432cb428f0cd36"}, {"id": "d06dab6d-dee5-3053-8019-56ded79ddf16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "ed308f24-9d07-3fa2-af8a-431f6f65c8c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <f60ec3058a85447008b88b762c859d336163acb3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "21c4ded0-1cfe-3803-8e5a-aa9cc3c45e68", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}